  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DPRK DRR</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DPRK RC community-based programmes will be implemented in three provinces 13 counties and 12 communities in an integrated approach to strengthen its programmes based on existing needs and available funding with strong emphasis on longer-term sustainability. Community-based disaster risk reducation is a major priority of the DPRK RC disaster management programme. this component is aimed at improving the knowledge attitudes and practices of communities and local authorities towards disaster preparedness mitigation response capacity in hazard monitoring early warning and evacuation system. through the CBDRR DPRK RC intends to reach out to 200 000 people focusing on capacity building of communities in the project implementation area NS staff and volunteers in the 12 communities within the integrated programme. The DPRK RC has an estimated one million members (including 100 000 volunteers and 300 000 Red Cross Youth) with a network of ten provincial branches and 200 city/county branches with volunteer bases. Operational provinces are North and South Hwanghae South Hamgyong North and South Phyongan. In case of emergency the NS has been able to work also elsewhere in country.</narrative>
  </description>
